paid-job-name = { $job }
    Paid role — { $price }
paid-job-priority-notice = [color=yellow][bold]Paid role — { $price } per spawn.[/bold][/color]
    With High priority and Ready status, this amount is automatically deducted from your character's personal account when you spawn at round start, if you have sufficient funds and a slot is available.
    Never, Low and Medium priorities do not authorize automatic payment.
paid-job-tooltip = Paid role. Joining deducts { $price } from your character's personal bank account. Automatic assignment when ready requires high priority, sufficient funds and an available slot. Each spawn requires payment. The entry fee is refunded if spawning fails.
paid-job-insufficient-funds = Your character's personal bank account has insufficient funds to join this paid role.
paid-job-selection-required = Set high priority for automatic assignment to a paid role. You can also select the role manually after the round starts. Entry requires sufficient funds in your character's personal account and an available slot.
paid-job-unavailable = This paid role is currently unavailable: no free slot or spawn point.
paid-job-purchased = { $price } was deducted from your character's personal bank account to join this paid role.

job-name-syndicate-operative = Syndicate Operative
JobSyndicateOperative = Syndicate Operative
job-description-syndicate-operative = A paid operative role in Omicron. Requires 20 hours of overall playtime. Enter a codename without a rank in the role settings, or leave it blank for a random codename. The Operative prefix is added automatically. Spawning on Bravo when ready requires high priority, sufficient funds and an available slot. Other priorities never cause automatic assignment. You can select the role manually after the round starts. Follow the Syndicate ghost role rules.
job-supervisors-syndicate-operative = Syndicate command and your sergeant
company-name-syndicate = Syndicate
